Pre-commit negative evidence is retained in the handoff: shorthand mechanism references initially violated the full-ID schema and were corrected; two invalid high-consequence fixtures were corrected to schema-valid MissionContracts.

## Current reality

- compiler: locally tested, canonical CI pending;
- zero-trust profile: **DESIGN_ONLY / NOT ENFORCED**;
- dynamic advantage: **UNKNOWN**;
- runtime composition: unresolved between PR #70 and #87;
- Verified Durable Mission Closures: **0 -> 0**;
- CVO/HARDENED/LIVE: unchanged and not claimed.

## Blockers after this PR

- canonical CI/review and stacked adoption;
- runtime-owner decision (#70 vs #87);
- sealed development/held-out/negative-control corpus and independent reviewer;
- actual canonical DALEOBANKS/WMI adapters;
- runtime composition of identity, attenuation, freshness, evaluator independence, receipts, and recovery;
- production key custody/distributed revocation;
- hardware attestation and external witness if a bounded threat model later requires them;
- a separate founder-authorized Phase-4 deliberation.

## Rollback

Close this draft, or revert the Phase-3 schema/compiler/dependency/tests/docs while retaining the inspection, deliberation, dissent, and failed evidence. PR #90 and static DurableWorkflow remain unchanged.

## Kill conditions

Kill/reconfigure if this slice emits an event, invokes a runtime/model/network/Gate, creates a parallel authority/truth system, changes mission authority or resource ceilings, bypasses evaluation, admits evidence-gated forms, removes the static/do-not alternatives, treats identity/digest/score as authority or truth, or claims rogue-proof/LIVE/PROVEN/HARDENED/autonomous regeneration.

## Review request

Review the fail-closed semantic boundary, cumulative ownership map, v1.0 compatibility, deterministic score trace, negative controls, supply-chain risk, and explicit refusal to execute. Do not merge or deploy from this PR.

## Canonical CI result

